# spec/ext/BudgetKey.constants: the constants BudgetKey.tla adds to the kernel's (T6).
# One line each: NAME  KIND  MEANING
Sessions    set of strings   the session identifiers a request may carry (what the engine's session scope counts)
Tenants     set of strings   tenant identifiers; a budget key's tenant is one of these and nothing else
Principals  set of strings   principal identifiers (the caller acting for the tenant)
Purposes    set of strings   purpose identifiers (what the money is for)
Windows     set of strings   whole days, written YYYY-MM-DD; a budget key's window is one day
# Kernel constants a model sets as well (KamanuKernel, KamanuPolicies):
#   Templates  set of [tool, amt, key |-> [session, budget]], amt in cents
#   Permit     one of PRespBasis, PReqBasis, PReqBasisNR, PRefundOnError, PRefundOnReconcile
#   Scope      ScopeSessionOnly (the engine's session-scoped limit) or ScopeBudget (a ledger keyed by the budget key)
#   Cap        cents (50000 is $500)
#   MaxReq, MaxFails, Reflexive, DenyRecord, Atomic, Lag, Faults, HasReconcile as in the kernel
